Where the Year Goes
Made entirely in code. No stock footage, no generated video, no generated images, no third-party
pictures, recordings or data of any kind.

EVIDENCE
  Two documents supplied by the client, and the figures stated inside them:
    · Atlanta Design Festival 2027 — Direction for the twentieth year. September 2026, 18 slides.
    · A festival convenes. It does not produce. October 2026, 6 slides.
  Pages of both are shown as evidence frames, rendered from the client's own PDFs at 150 dpi and
  graded to greyscale. Quoted lines are typeset as transcriptions and labelled as such.
  Every claim, with its source page and the wording it comes from, is listed in FACTS.md, along
  with the three inferences the film makes and marks on screen.

  The production calendar is a schematic reading, not a record: the documents state that each
  produced event takes months of build but give no month-by-month schedule. The calendar carries
  SCHEMATIC on screen throughout.

TYPEFACES
  Archivo — Omnibus-Type — SIL Open Font License 1.1
  IBM Plex Mono — IBM — SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Source Serif 4 — Adobe — SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Licence texts ship beside the fonts in fonts/. All three are used as the style names them:
  a grotesque for findings, mono for tags and readouts, serif italic for quoted wording.

VOICE
  Kokoro (kokoro-onnx), voice am_michael, run locally and offline. Synthetic narration, not a
  recording of a person. The script is in lines.json and the subtitles in film.json.

  Note: the speech-to-text check the pipeline normally runs on every line could not run in the
  environment this was built in, because the Whisper model host was unreachable. The script
  contains no digits, abbreviations or unusual spellings, and the subtitles carry the authoritative
  wording.

SOUND
  Score and foley synthesised in this project (mix.py) with numpy and scipy: bowed low strings,
  pizzicato, tremolo clusters, a resolving chord, a pendulum tick, and the print foley (paper,
  pencil, keystrokes, taps, a rubber stamp, a rewind sweep and one deep thump). No sample
  libraries, no recordings, no third-party audio.

PICTURE
  Drawn frame by frame with Canvas 2D in this project (film.js), captured headless and encoded
  with ffmpeg. Lemo-Opuscar supplies the render and audio tooling
  (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, code MIT); none of its demo material is in this film.

